{"title":"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems\">2002 AMC 12P #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">2002 AMC 10P #20</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(PIE)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (PIE)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many three-digit numbers have at least one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and at least one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d0860e9ed8577f3374ad05374a3a87438c1f4d93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }52 \\qquad \\text{(B) }54  \\qquad \\text{(C) }56 \\qquad \\text{(D) }58 \\qquad \\text{(E) }60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can do this problem with some simple case work.\n</p><p>Case 1: The hundreds place is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />\nThis means that the tens place and ones place must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. This case covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/218ecb90c544e073be81c79d161050daa08e0ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/1288f16f77606bb83db76df0877615ef6e8b149e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> so it gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc6504874eea6b913d2861882643c9cbd94c792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 7 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> cases.\n</p><p>Case 2: The hundreds place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be in the tens place or ones place. Starting with cases in which the tens place is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e8dee5e045466a6b8147a0f9a4db01ee4c5e78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$203, 213, 223, 243, 253, 263, 273, 283,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3573b2f452b7f54d5d7eb639da98f05192696288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$293.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />  With cases in which the tens place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/facfc32a55426e7f3f4b6fa4de1ecd66e35147e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$230-239$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> more cases. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078fe3fe5a9ec4e76ff3955f112b64ca834d8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 10=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> cases.\n</p><p>Case 3: The hundreds place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />\nThis case is almost identical to the second case, just swap the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s in the reasoning and it's the same, giving us an additional <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases.\n</p><p>Adding up all of these cases gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8dfcc7573fd18ac59265895dc228b8d024967c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14+19+19=52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" /> cases, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbee9fb94b1f8e47f7fee08b47d7b00117a15df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }52}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"72\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28PIE.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(PIE)\">Solution 2 (PIE)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (PIE)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can solve this problem with the principle of inclusion-exclusion. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c2f362fa9963653ac3062512ba7b34026d3735a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\#(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of three-digit numbers without the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4b101dc358c2decdb946ba00f9e50ff1a2ac14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\#(B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of three-digit numbers without the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badd03e9e9d2d27198b2eb7c56ab0cf30b687c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\#(A \\cap B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of three-digit numbers without digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd696bc462a2dc84ba3fc9d03c2fbf8fa0b6a52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\#(A)=\\#(B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> by symmetry. We use constructive counting to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e6487c2b3f23358b18af915e1be2b57ecaeeeefe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\#(A) = 8 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 9 = 648\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e49ed68c23d43c8bba3f0c353a9992fbb202825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\#(A) = \\#(B) = 648$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d89748a7aaadb4a3642da212db2de54be0ab009.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\#(A \\cap B) = 7 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 8 = 448.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Hence, by PIE, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e25b14191600052bb2f8077794fb48cf42aabfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\#(A \\cup B) = \\#(A) + \\#(B) - \\#(A \\cap B) = 648 + 648 - 448 = 848\\]\" width=\"511\" height=\"18\" /> so the count of three-digit numbers that do not have a digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or a digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9ebdb3ac40d384ca766da4c8f4bcf22dd66979e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\#(A \\cup B) = 848$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281df5260bd50d9d56cd3a9c3067cb2e640316ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 10 = 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" /> ways to construct a three-digit number in total, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b055022c6006705a1dcb85ac4c7f88385ad3707a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900 - 848 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }52}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"168\" height=\"30\" /> numbers that have at least one of digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~ Math-lover1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P\">2002 AMC 10P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redire